Table 1 summarizes the properties of the three discovered pulsars. PSR J1746-2850I and PSR J1746-2850II were discovered in the same survey pointing and were confirmed with the Green Bank Telescope in June 2008; subsequent monthly timing observations at 2 GHz are ongoing. We observed both pulsars at 1.5 and 4.8 GHz with the dual goals of estimating their spectral indices and improving their position measurements. We also observed PSR J1946-2850I at 9 GHz in order to confirm that its relatively flat spectrum extends to higher frequencies. PSR J1745-2910 was discovered in February 2009 and will be timed starting in June 2009. Profiles of the three pulsars are shown in Figure 2.

